constraints:
1 ≤ N ≤ 10^{5}
1 ≤ A[i] ≤ 10^{6}
1 ≤ Q ≤ 10^{4}
1 ≤ C ≤ 10^{9}
0 ≤ K ≤ 10
1 ≤ Queries[i][j] ≤ N, j>1

expected time complexity: O(NLogMx + Q*K*LogMx + Q*(LogMx)^{2})
expected auxiliary space: O(Mx)

standard_solution_code:
class Solution:

	def maximumToys(self, N, A, Q, Queries):
		toys = sorted(((item, i + 1) for (i, item) in enumerate(A)))
		output = []
		for item in Queries:
			banned = set(item[2:])
			money = item[0]
			count = 0
			for (cost, toy) in toys:
				if cost > money:
					break
				if not toy in banned:
					money -= cost
					count += 1
			output.append(count)
		return output
